'''Houston Jerami Grant''' ({{IPAc-en|ˈ|dʒ|ɛr|ə|m|i}} {{respell|JERR|ə|mee}};<ref>{{cite press release |author=<!--Not stated--> |title=2023-24 start of season NBA pronunciation guide
 |url=https://www.nba.com/news/2023-24-start-of-season-nba-pronunciation-guide |publisher=National Basketball Association |date=October 24, 2023 |access-date=May 18, 2024}}</ref> born March 12, 1994) is an American professional [[basketball]] player for the [[Portland Trail Blazers]] of the [[National Basketball Association]] (NBA). He played [[college basketball]] for the [[Syracuse Orange men's basketball|Syracuse Orange]] and was drafted by the [[Philadelphia 76ers]] in the second round of the [[2014 NBA draft]]. Grant has also played for the [[Oklahoma City Thunder]], [[Denver Nuggets]], and [[Detroit Pistons]]. He won a gold medal with the [[2020 United States men's Olympic basketball team|2020 U.S. Olympic team]].

